<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Algarve</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Algarve is the southernmost region of mainland Portugal, a coastal strip between the Atlantic and the hills of the Serra de Monchique and Serra do Caldeirão. Its name comes from the Arabic al-Gharb, 'the west', from the centuries of Muslim rule, and it was the last part of Portugal taken from the Moors, in 1249. Portuguese kings bore the separate title of King of the Algarve until 1910.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/algarve.jpg" alt="Algarve" width="320" height="218" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vitor Oliveira from Torres Vedras, PORTUGAL · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pal%C3%A1cio_de_Est%C3%B3i_-_Portugal_(8291585643)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
